.SH NAME
le-db - Read databases and create exclusive vendor-format backups


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle db [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicit single-endpoint database tools; no discovery or background jobs.
Supported engines: postgres, mysql, mariadb, mongodb, redis.
Query input comes from stdin only: one SQL read, Mongo JSON filter, or Redis JSON command array.
Use least-privilege read-only credentials via LOCALHOST_DB_USERNAME/PASSWORD and Varlock.
Remote connections require verified TLS. Literal loopback can use plaintext.
Query/schema results are limited to 1,000 rows and 1 MiB; requests to 64 KiB.
Privileged SQL functions and server-side effects are not sandboxed.
Backups on macOS/Linux require an independently installed trusted vendor utility and an absolute new output path.
Windows backups are unavailable pending process-tree containment support.
MySQL/MariaDB/Mongo backups also need an existing private vendor credentials file.
Redis backups cover ALL logical databases and may trigger BGSAVE. Restore tests remain your responsibility.


